      "content": "Absolutely, I can help with that. First, it's important to understand your demand variability and supply variability. A common formula for safety stock is: Safety Stock = Z-score x Standard Deviation of Lead Time Demand, where Z-score relates to your desired service level. This formula helps compensate for the variability in lead times, especially from inconsistent suppliers like Shenzhen. Don't forget to factor in your average lead time and daily demand rate when calculating the standard deviation of lead time demand. By implementing this formula, you can more effectively manage your buffer stock and mitigate stockouts.",
